<p>The woman first blew into a hand-held breathalyser and showed it produced a 0 blood alcohol level (BAL) reading as a control test.</p>
<p>She then took a bite of a hot cross bun and tried the test again on the same machine.</p>
<p>This time the screen showed a reading of 0.018 &#8211; meaning just two buns would probably produce a result of more than the UK legal limit of 0.08.</p>
